  "name": "@andrep1/infor-search-mcp",
  "readme": "# Infor Search MCP Server\n\nAn [MCP](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server that gives AI agents search access to Infor resources:\n\n- **`search_docs`** \u2014 the official Infor documentation library ([docs.infor.com](https://docs.infor.com)): product guides, release notes, configuration and how-to articles.\n- **`search_community`** \u2014 the Infor Developer Community ([community.infor.com](https://community.infor.com)): discussions, Q&A, workarounds, and real-world solutions.\n\nNeither endpoint requires user-provided authentication \u2014 both use publicly accessible APIs.\n\nBuilt with TypeScript on [Node.js](https://nodejs.org), using the [`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@modelcontextprotocol/sdk).\n\n## Requirements\n\n- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) 18 or newer\n\n## Connecting an MCP client\n\nThe published package ships an executable, so your MCP client can launch it directly with `npx` \u2014 no manual install or path wrangling needed.\n\n### Kiro (`.kiro/settings/mcp.json`) or Claude Desktop\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"infor-search\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"@andrep1/infor-search-mcp\"],\n      \"disabled\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`npx -y @andrep1/infor-search-mcp` downloads (and caches) the latest published version and runs it over stdio. The client manages the process lifecycle; you don't start it by hand.\n\n## Local development\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build       # compile TypeScript to dist/\nnpm run start       # node dist/index.js\n```\n\nYou should see `Infor Search MCP server running on stdio` on stderr. It then waits for JSON-RPC messages on stdin.\n\nTo point an MCP client at a local build instead of the published package, use an absolute path to the compiled entry:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"infor-search\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\"/path/to/infor-search-mcp/dist/index.js\"],\n      \"disabled\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Tools\n\n### `search_docs`\n\nSearch the official Infor documentation.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `query` | string (required) | Search query, e.g. `\"M3 API transactions\"`. |\n| `product` | string | Filter by product name, e.g. `\"Infor M3 Core\"`, `\"Infor OS\"`. |\n| `limit` | number (1\u201350) | Max results (default: 10). |\n| `full` | boolean | Return full page body text instead of highlight snippets (default: false). |\n\n### `search_community`\n\nSearch the Infor Developer Community.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n|-----------|------|-------------|\n| `query` | string (required) | Search query, e.g. `\"XtendM3 extension\"`. |\n| `category` | enum | Filter by category (see table below). |\n| `sort` | enum | `relevance` (default), `dateInserted`, `dateUpdated`. |\n| `limit` | number (1\u201350) | Max results (default: 10). |\n| `type` | enum | `discussion` or `comment`. Omit for both. |\n\n#### Community categories\n\n| Name | ID | Description |\n|------|----|-------------|\n| `developer` | 61 | Developer Community (all subcategories) |\n| `infor-os` | 7 | Infor OS Platform Forums |\n| `integration` | 8 | Integration (ION, BODs, Data Lake) |\n| `api-gateway` | 10 | API Gateway |\n| `ion-connect` | 11 | ION Connect |\n| `ion-desk` | 12 | ION Desk |\n| `data-lake` | 51 | Data Fabric / Data Lake |\n| `portal` | 29 | Portal and Workspaces |\n| `m3` | 124 | M3 Development (Hubs) |\n| `syteline` | 84 | SyteLine Development |\n| `general` | 39 | General Developer Forum |\n\n## Prompts\n\nThe server also exposes a reusable **prompt** \u2014 a pre-built template that MCP clients typically surface as a slash command.\n\n| Prompt | Arguments | What it does |\n|--------|-----------|--------------|\n| `search_infor` | `query` (required) | Researches a topic across both the docs and the community, then synthesizes a cited answer. |\n\n## Project structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  index.ts                 MCP server: registers tools + prompts, stdio transport\n  prompts.ts               The search_infor prompt (docs + community research)\n  format.ts                Formats raw API responses into agent-friendly text\n  search/\n    docs-search.ts         searchDocs() against docs.infor.com\n    community-search.ts    searchCommunity() against community.infor.com\n    product-catalog.ts     Validates/resolves the docs `product` filter\n```\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev         # tsc --watch\nnpm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit\nnpm run build       # compile to dist/\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The docs API obtains a short-lived bearer token via a public client key; the token is cached in-process and refreshed automatically.\n- All logging goes to **stderr** to avoid corrupting the stdio JSON-RPC stream on stdout.\n",
